  [1mShort design[0m

  [1m[38;5;153mapp.js[39m — one file, four small changes:[0m

  1. [1mNew helper [38;5;153mgetTrackingId()[0m above [38;5;153mlogin[39m. Reads key [38;5;153mlogin_tracking_id[39m from [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m; if absent, generates one
     with [38;5;153mcrypto.randomUUID()[39m, writes it back, and returns it. Wrapped in [38;5;153mtry/catch[39m — [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m throws in some
     private-browsing modes and under [38;5;153mfile://[39m in a few browsers, and an analytics ID should never be what breaks the
     login form. On failure it falls back to a module-scoped ID that lives for the page session only.
  2. [1mSignature becomes [38;5;153mlogin(username, password, userId)[39m.[0m Third position, so the existing positional arguments don't
     shift and the one call site is the only thing that has to change. It stays required-by-convention rather than
     defaulted: a silently-missing tracking ID produces tracking data with holes in it, which is worse than a visible
     [38;5;153mundefined[39m in the log.
  3. [1m[38;5;153mlogin[39m uses it[0m — includes [38;5;153muserId[39m in its log line and in the returned object ([38;5;153m{ success: true, user: username, userId
[39m     [38;5;153m}[39m), so the caller and the eventual API POST both have it.
  4. [1mCall site at line 23[0m passes [38;5;153mgetTrackingId()[39m.

  [1mNot touching:[0m [38;5;153mindex.html[39m (no new form field — the ID is generated, not typed), [38;5;153msrc/[39m, [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m, or [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m.

  [1mWhat this is and isn't:[0m the ID identifies a [3mbrowser[0m, not a person. Clearing site data or switching devices yields a
  new one, and two people sharing a machine share it. That's the honest ceiling on "track who logged in" without a
  backend — worth knowing before tracking code downstream treats it as a user identity.

  [1mTesting:[0m no harness exists, so verification is manual — open [38;5;153mindex.html[39m, submit the form, confirm the console shows a
  UUID; reload and submit again, confirm the same UUID; clear [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m, confirm a new one. I can set up a test
